[{:adr/fourth-distinct-operating-states-shape-3510 "'3510''s own registry-declared operating-states (:intake :observe :recommend :dispatch :settle :audit) is a FOURTH genuinely distinct shape for this fleet's own :spec-authoring scope, after the services shape (securityops/8010 etc.), the manufacturing shape (meddeviceops/2660, basicchemops/2011) and the permit-based construction/trade shape (electricalops/4321, plumbingops/4322). This one is a grid-operations/market-settlement lifecycle: observe telemetry -> recommend a dispatch action -> dispatch -> settle (wheeling/interconnection charges) -- a structurally different governed decision point (a dispatch that could violate a grid reliability standard) from any prior pick. Legacy placeholder :repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-D3510) confirmed via direct GitHub API 404 check to never have actually existed. No bespoke capability library exists for grid transmission/distribution specifically", :adr/explicit-scope-note-3510 "the README's own text carries an explicit 'Scope note: transmission/distribution, not generation' section naming cloud-itonami-isic-3512 directly and explaining the value-chain distinction -- following the SAME discipline foodserviceops/5610 established when distinguishing itself from the existing accommodation vertical, and hazwasteops/3812 established when distinguishing itself from the two existing waste-adjacent verticals", :adr/related ["2607101600-cloud-itonami-plumbing-4322-blueprint" "2607101500-cloud-itonami-electrical-4321-blueprint" "2607101400-cloud-itonami-basicchem-2011-blueprint" "2607100300-cloud-itonami-missionops-9900-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511 through 9900 ADR-0001s (106 prior actors)" "langgraph ADR-0001"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607101800", :adr/real-repo-naming-3510 "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-3510 (public, matching every prior vertical's own visibility), following the SAME cloud-itonami-isic-#### convention as all 114 prior/sibling actors, rather than the legacy D####-prefixed placeholder scheme. business-id updated from 'cloud-itonami-D3510' to 'cloud-itonami-3510' to match", :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 8, :spec 532, :total 646}", :adr/deferral-resolved-lesson-3510 "confirms that a candidate deferred multiple rounds in a row can still be resolved cleanly once the right distinguishing framing is found -- the deferral itself (rather than a rushed, under-justified pick) bought the time needed to arrive at a genuinely defensible scope", :adr/test-status-3510 "kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 162 assertions, all green", :adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 9, :spec 531, :total 646}", :adr/fresh-governor-no-collision-3510 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/governor keyword, :grid-transmission-governor, is grep-verified UNIQUE fleet-wide -- distinct from cloud-itonami-isic-3512's own :grid-policy-governor, a deliberate choice not to reuse a similar-sounding keyword from a directly adjacent vertical", :adr/date "2026-07-09", :adr/blueprint-only-artifacts-3510 "published README.md, blueprint.edn, docs/business-model.md, docs/operator-guide.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE (AGPL-3.0-or-later, verbatim) -- SAME artifact set as every prior fresh-blueprint publication this scope. Deliberately NO src/test/deps.edn/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md", :adr/ninth-spec-authoring-build "NINTH 'author a new blueprint from :spec tier' build, resolves the longest-standing deferred candidate: '3510' (Electric power generation, transmission and distribution) was first flagged at ADR-2607101400, deferred again implicitly at ADR-2607101500 and ADR-2607101600, each time pending careful distinguishing framing against cloud-itonami-isic-3512's own adjacent territory", :adr/registry-field-replacement-3510 "the existing '3510' registry entry had its :repo, :business-id and :optional-technologies fields updated, and its explicit :maturity :spec override REMOVED so maturity/maturity-of now auto-derive :blueprint from the real :repo presence", :db/id -1, :adr/resolving-the-deferral-3510 "cloud-itonami-isic-3512 ('Community Renewable Energy Operations', :implemented, :grid-policy-governor) covers community-scale electricity GENERATION -- a solar/wind cooperative. '3510''s own ISIC Rev.4 class text is broader ('generation, transmission AND distribution'), exactly the redundancy risk flagged earlier. Resolved by scoping the blueprint EXPLICITLY to the transmission/distribution ('wires') side of the value chain -- substations, transmission lines, distribution feeders, interconnection and wheeling-service management -- a business genuinely distinct from generation in most real electricity markets (FERC regulates transmission federally in the US while generation is often merchant/competitive; Japan's 電気事業法 separately licenses 送配電事業者 from 発電事業者; UK licenses DNOs -- Distribution Network Operators -- separately from generators; Germany's EnWG separately regulates Übertragungsnetzbetreiber/Verteilnetzbetreiber from Erzeuger). Real, well-precedented distinction, not a forced one", :adr/west-registration-deliberately-not-done-3510 "same established precedent as every prior fresh-blueprint build this scope: none of the cloud-itonami-isic-* repos are registered as west projects. cloud-itonami-isic-3510 follows suit -- no :extra-projects/west.yml entry", :adr/blueprint-count-updated-again-3510 "ADR-2607101600's own (is (= 8 (:blueprint m))) assertion updated to (is (= 9 (:blueprint m))), continuing the 'not a fixed invariant' framing ADR-2607100500 established. Added a live-state corroboration assertion ((is (= :blueprint (industry/maturity \"3510\")))) alongside the eight prior live-state corroboration tests and the synthetic-fixture-based unit test", :adr/next-steps-3510 "cloud-itonami-isic-3510 joins the eight prior fresh-blueprint picks as a 